WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.800
Cybersecurity training. Module 9. When something goes wrong.

2
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.933
Many incidents are noticed first by the person involved.

3
00:00:09.933 --> 00:00:14.100
Treat the signs as worth reporting even when you are not sure.

4
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:20.267
At minute zero you notice something wrong. Stop what you are doing.

5
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:25.200
Within minutes, tell your lead and HR. Do not wait to be sure.

6
00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:30.633
Within the hour, write down the facts: what, when and which system. Keep evidence.

7
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.400
As instructed, change passwords, sign out sessions or isolate the device.

8
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.267
Report straight away.

9
00:00:39.633 --> 00:00:42.867
Keep the message or file as it is.

10
00:00:43.167 --> 00:00:45.567
Do not try to fix it quietly.

11
00:00:45.933 --> 00:00:49.567
Do not delete the message or reply to the attacker.

12
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.000
What happened.

13
00:00:52.333 --> 00:00:54.667
When it happened and when you noticed.

14
00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:58.233
Where: which system, and how it was sent.

15
00:00:58.567 --> 00:01:01.667
And what you have done so far, and not done.

16
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:03.667
Pause.

17
00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:04.900
Verify.

18
00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:06.367
Report fast.

19
00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:08.500
Now read the module.
